{"seq":1,"mint":"C4","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":true,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"rule 1 is membership in `ungrounded_claims` (no evidence record at all for the claim id) and rule 2 is membership in `out_of_proof` (records exist, all with a digest differing from `sha256_hex(claim.proposition)`)","clause_quoted":true,"facts":[],"why":"The `stale` partition excludes records with an empty digest, but `out_of_proof` is emitted whenever there is a stale record and `fresh` is empty. Thus a claim with both a differing-digest record and an empty-digest record can enter `out_of_proof`, even though not all of its records have a digest differing from the current proposition.","quoted":false,"rejected_span":"let (fresh, stale): (Vec<&&EvidenceRecord>, Vec<&&EvidenceRecord>) = records\n            .iter()\n            .filter(|r| !r.proposition_digest.is_empty())\n            .partition(|r| r.proposition_digest == current); \n\n        for r in &stale {\n            let line = format!(\n                \"{} — evidence from pass {} graded different text than this claim now carries \\\n(recorded digest {}…, current {}…).\\\\n      that pass said: {} — {}\",\n                claim.id,\n                r.pass,\n                &r.proposition_digest[..r.proposition_digest.len().min(12)],\n                &current[..current.len().min(12)],\n                r.verdict,\n                r.note.as_deref().unwrap_or(\"(no note)\"),\n            );\n            if fresh.is_empty() {\n                out_of_proof.push(format!(\n\nA record with no digest at all predates the field. It is\n        // treated as grading the current text rather than dropped:"}],"at":1790111987,"cost":0.009101640000000001,"elapsed_ms":56648,"attempts":5,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0,"typed_versions":["jev-1.13.0"],"gate_calls":1,"typed_classify_calls":1,"typed_literal_calls":1}
